               <h4>Why We Need New Technology for Workforce Automation?</h4>
Management of employees includes marking their attendance, expense management , job allocation, shift rotation, leave management and of course keeping check if they are present on work location or not. This task of <b>Field Employee Tracking</b> is a major step in retail and online businesses which is not possible without employing comprehensive <b>workforce management software.</b> In addition to this, data like total number of employees working across the city and country is relevant to the organization. Handling all these things manually is a very old school and conventional way of <b>field force management.</b> This may cause a lot of discrepancies along with the requirement of additional staff to keep check on them.</p><p>

Not only is this method tedious and time consuming, but also ends up being more expensive for organizations. Since records are maintained on paper, there is always some probability of errors, frauds or missing out information.</p><p>

<h4>What Is the Solution?</h4>
Since we are living in a modern era, the approach in our solutions should also be new and updated. Using latest technologies may prove very useful and time efficient. GPS (Global Positioning System) is one such promising technology which helps us with <b>location tracking and location intelligence.</b> Location tracking is basically used to determine the physical location of a person or an object and records its movement digitally with the help of a GPS chip which is generally embedded in smartphone. So why not use such a gem in solving out the existing manual troubles. Various successful corporations are using this by including a <b>field force tracking</b> system that is based on smart maps and additionally embedded with location intelligence and location analytics. It not only keeps track of movement of employees but also shares the location of team members with one another.</p><p>

One of the most trusted and widely used workforce management solutions IMPRINT has already embedded this technology in their Sales force management software. This GPS embedded solution has proven to be a boon in field force performance monitoring, resulting in enhanced productivity.</p><p>

1) Its automated attendance feature works on GPS sensors which connects the employee’s smart phone to the satellite and thus based on employee’s current location, it marks the attendance. This is one of the most loved features of IMPRINT, as it is extremely useful for the in-store and field workforce management.</p><p>

2) With automated attendance, the data of employees can be easily collected and is helpful for instant decision making.</p><p>

3) In case any employee wants to take leave, they can simply apply on portal .Their work can be allocated to another employee in advance without wasting much time.</p><p>

4) For the field employees, this location intelligence software helps in determining the nearest client, as soon as it detects client or agent nearby, it sends an alert. This way client meeting can be scheduled instantly. This not only cuts the unnecessary travel expenses but also improves employee’s efficiency.</p><p>

